{"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L89","fileName":"NontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE37nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponentsSays10ArraySliceVy6VertexQzGGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through both."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successors."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The components are those of ","type":"text"},{"code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" without the trivial ones, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. Empty exactly when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in ","type":"text"},{"code":"attractingComponents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices do not start at 0.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":", so one sort by that vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position puts the components in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", where positions are insertion order:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(V + E).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/nontrivialstronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"title":"Vertex","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"i